**Thesren** (/' *tɛsrən* /, *[[lucran|Lucran]]*: 𓐌 𓍣 𓈪 𓐢𓁫 𓈪 𓈅 ) is one of the seven elemental deities. He is bound to the element of Light and he is the god of inspiration and love. The Thesrec[^thesrec] religion conducts it's religion in the open, but is very gated on the inside.

-----

# Religion
The Thesrec[^thesrec] religion is centered on the power and effects of Light. Different from the other religion, the Thesrec holds them self as the highest and most righteous of them all.

The Thesrec churches are large stone building built in population centers. They feature many spires and large windows. In the entrance-way there is a mosaic telling a local prophecy or legend. The roofs are large so-called onion domes. and each one of the spires holds a smaller identical version. Usually these are topped with a Igen star, but most have eroded since construction and haven't been replaced.

The Thesrec are part of the elite side of society. Mostly consisting of Magistrates and Justices. They can manage to maintain these massive churches, statues of their legends and the mosaics in tip-top state.  The communion has evolved in this very stoic ritual, in which appearance has become the main focus. The communal reciting of poems and long monologues from the residing priest are prime examples of its fall into tradition.

The ideas are very much centered around the maintaining of the status quo. The control of the justice system, the system of government and the massive amount of wealth are all symbols of their control over society.  The "Ever-Shining Light" is seen in completely different light after accounting for these facts.

As the archivists will tell you, Thesren must be really old deity. There are none surviving stories of ascension, which suggests he has always had control over the light domain. This is as the Thesrec like to believe, but there is some evidence of a predecessor. As there are old scrolls mention a deity of light, yet the names are missing. But in these scrolls they are referred to by she/her pronouns, alluring to a predecessor.

## Sects
Different Sects/Cults
* Heka of **Maat**
The Heka of Maat is focused on the maintaining of the natural flow of the world and the status quo. They are organized in the Circle of Destiny chivalric order. 
* Heka of **Heteb**
Heteb is the Heka of justice and law. This Heka is occupied by the justices and many other in the legal systems across the world. Scales a re an import symbolical part of this Heka
* Heka of **Nefr**
Nefr is the Heka of beauty and appearance. Their ideals have influenced a large part of the beauty ideals in the Thesrec religion.
* Heka of **Mer**
The Heka of Mer is an isolated part of the Thesrec religion. It is here, where the festival of Amodesia[^amodesia] originated. The beliefs of Mer clash with many oither more conservative ideals of the other Thesrec.

## Structure
### Venerated Ancestors
*See also: [[list-of-thesrec-venerated-ancestors|List of Thesrec Venerated Ancestors]]*
The Thesrec[^thesrec] have a lot of venerated ancestors. From old legends to recent heroes are honored by the Thesrec. In Thesrec dominated areas, these ancestors are everywhere. They are addressed by the *Trin*[^trin] prefix, which is given to them posthumously.
### Priestly Order
The Thesrec[^thesrec] religion is one with heavily defined ranks of priest. The higher ranks want to prevent anyone gain a huge amount of power within the church. It is one of the only religion to have a Head of Faith, the *Hanta* [^hanta].

Rank|Description
--|--
Hanta | Head of Faith
Antun | Cardinal *Obal*
Obal | All the churches in a nation
Anamnen | Multiple churches in an area
Ictesis | A singular church
%%Rank names are from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liturgy_of_Addai_and_Mari]%%
# Cultural
## Amodesia
Amodesia[^amodesia] is a festival of love, originating in the Heka of Mer. The festival has outgrown it's status of local festival and in time will outgrow it status of Holy Day. Right now it sits as a more universal and lovely version of the Lightfall Solstice, featuring the same wine and branches, but having a theme love, pink and festival.

## Lightfall Solstice
The Thesrec[^thesrec] is unique in it's two holy days. There is the Lightfall Solstice, which is held in the upmost importance. Yet in fact it is a stoic ritual communion, made special by the induction of new members. Otherwise it features large bowls of ritual wine and burning a olive branch.

## Pars Alba
The Pars Alba[^pars] is the holy book of Thesren. It describes the way to live, with "real world" examples. The stories range from futuristic dreams to past choices. The pages of the book itself are translucent and contain no lettering directly, but the Thesrec[^thesrec] have pioneered a way of lighting up these pages and revealing the lettering.

## Lucran
*See also: [[lucran|Lucran]]*
The Lucran[^lucran] or *Ra'mdt*[^ra'mdt] language is a ancient language of glyphs. It is used by the Thesrec[^thesrec] elite to hide the true nature of their religion. The glyphs can be magically activated as Runes.

